<title>POLAND: KPW clears Polish metals firm Hutmen for trade.</title>
<headline>KPW clears Polish metals firm Hutmen for trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade the initial public offering of up to 370,000 shares and state treasury sale of 1,979,224 shares in non-ferrous metals maker  Hutmen SA, the KPW said.</p>
<p>The KPW said in a statement on Wednesday that Hutmen, which seeks a main market bourse listing, currently has a total of 2,474,030 shares, all held by the state treasury and all approved for public trade.</p>
<p> IPO Tranches	    No Of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>			     Offered		  Period</p>
<p> Open			280,000		  June 30-July 4</p>
<p> Small-investor	   90,000		  June 16-25</p>
<p> State sale tranche  1,979,224		  May 15-27</p>
<p> Lead Manager:	Powszechny Bank Kredyowy SA (PBK) brokerage</p>
<p> Use Of Proceeds:   complete the firm's privatisation,</p>
<p>			  investment in production machinery</p>
<p> EARNINGS DATA	   1996 H1	  1995</p>
<p>(in million of PLN)  Net profit:	     4.0	     13.0</p>
<p> Sales:		  180.3	    283.9</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
